---
description: Follow these rules when making Twig components.
globs: 
---
Use Twig as templating language. Put it in templates/_components directory. Do not apply any css classes. Use the following as example markup. Always put a class prop on the root element.

<example>
{# @var string|null class #}
{% set class = class ?? null %}

{# @var string|null href #}
{% set href = href ?? null %}

{# @var string|null title #}
{% set title = title ?? null %}

{# @var string|null description #}
{% set description = description ?? null %}

{# Computed values #}
{% set element = href ? 'a' : 'article' %}
{% set headingElement = "h#{headingLevel}" %}

<a href="{{ href }}" class="{{ cx(class) }}">
    {% if title %}
      <h2>{{ title }}</h2>
    {% endif %}
    {% if description %}
      <p>{{ description }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</a>

</example>